            <div xml:id="d613">

                <pb facs="0593" n="427" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg427"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 337.11/450</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 20, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>American Consul Santiago reports interior conditions not improved; that Santiago
                    de Cuba is full of American refugees; that everything on plantations of Cuba
                    Company is destroyed, Paso Estancia burned and managers Palmarito reported
                    expecting destruction of their property any moment. He states the Government
                    troops are there but they are insufficient for protection. Present these facts
                    to Menocal Government and report to Department attitude Cuban Government in this
                    connection. You may say to President Menocal that this Government insists upon
                    adequate protection for these properties.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
